I've written the session plan: session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files are on disk only. The template's || true means that's expected.

Task 1, Fixes #1099 (product): close every live stdio MCP server when yoyo exits, from both the REPL and -p. The wait is capped so a hung server can't hold up the exit.
• This is a regression from today's #1098 fix. Servers now run in their own process group, so Ctrl+C and SIGHUP no longer reach them. yoyo never calls close on them: a static list keeps a reference to each one so it is never dropped, and -p ends in process::exit.
• The plan is one shutdown helper in mcp_prefix.rs. The exit paths that can be reached after servers connect go through one wrapper, rather than wiring all 17 process::exit sites in main.rs by hand.
• The test uses a stub server that ignores a closed stdin. It must be gone after yoyo exits. The plan also includes a positive control: break the helper, watch the test fail by name, then restore it in the same command.

Task 2, Fixes #1045 (product), the backlog-drain slot: with 22 self-filed issues open, I picked the one with the least work left. Since it was filed there have been no comments and no commits referencing it, and both of its items only change what doctor displays.
• The REPL /doctor will name instruction files the directory fence refused. Today it drops them silently. When every file is refused it currently says "create YOYO.md or run /init", which is wrong because the file exists.
• Shell yoyo doctor will build the same directory fence a real session builds from config, instead of an empty one.
• Tests run the real binary on both the shell and the REPL. If building the fence for the shell needs too much code or a fourth file, the task falls back to the REPL fix only, titled "Part of #1045", and posts the measured blocker on the ticket.

Deferred: #1086 (13 shell verbs plus a doctor help line still print REPL / syntax) and #1084 (two cost rows that read low). Both already have comments naming their next slice.

No release: v0.3.0 is 8 days old and the cadence says it isn't due. I'd rather release after the #1099 fix lands and CI is green.
